<title>USA: Motorola unveils dual GSM/PCS cell phone.</title>
<headline>Motorola unveils dual GSM/PCS cell phone.</headline>
<dateline>SCHAUMBURG, Ill. 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc said Thursday it unveiled its new dual-band cellular phone for use with Global System for Mobile Communications (GSM) and Personal Communications Services (PCS) networks.</p>
<p>At an exhibition in Germany, the company said the phone, called the International 8800, will allow worldwide users of GSM to use their phones on PCS 1900 systems in the United States.</p>
<p>The phone is expected to be available later this year, Motorola said.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
